.TH MURALD 1 "August 25, 2026" "mural 0.1.1" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
murald \- Wayland layer-shell wallpaper daemon
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B murald
.RB [ --socket
.IR PATH ]
.RB [ --trace ]
.RB [ --standalone ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B murald
starts a supervisor process that owns the public IPC socket, wallpaper state,
systemd readiness, and renderer health. The supervisor starts the same
executable as a renderer child, which creates one wlroots layer-shell
background surface per output and renders JPG, PNG, and WebP wallpapers through
EGL/GLES.
It is controlled over a Unix socket by
.BR muralctl (1)
and keeps native wallpaper library, history, favorites, quarantine, and
per-layout current-wall state.
.PP
On startup, murald displays the saved current wallpaper set. If no mural state
exists, it chooses and persists the first random set.
.PP
When the compositor exposes
.BR zwlr_output_power_manager_v1 ,
murald tracks per-output power state. If an output is definitely powered off,
murald defers EGL surface work, texture uploads, and swaps, then renders
pending wallpaper state after power returns. Unknown output-power state waits
for a definitive mode event; unsupported output-power management falls back to
normal rendering.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI --socket " PATH"
Listen on PATH instead of the default socket.
.TP
.B --standalone
Run the legacy single-process daemon for debugging.
.TP
.BR --trace , " --debug"
Enable verbose diagnostic logging to stderr/journal.
Per-frame render logging is suppressed unless
.B MURAL_TRACE_FRAMES
is also set.
.TP
.BR -V , " --version"
Print the Mural version and exit.
.TP
.BR -h , " --help"
Show command help and exit.
.SH CONFIGURATION
murald reads configuration from
.BR mural-config (5).
Some settings also have environment overrides; see
.BR mural-config (5)
for the supported keys.
.SH SYSTEMD
The packaged user service uses
.B Type=notify
and murald sends
.B READY=1
after the IPC socket is listening and startup wallpaper display has completed.
It sends
.B STOPPING=1
on normal shutdown.
.PP
The supervisor is the systemd main process. If the renderer child exits or
stops responding to the private control channel, the supervisor records a
diagnostic under the mural state directory when possible, starts a new renderer
generation, and restores the saved current wallpaper set.
.PP
The packaged unit enables systemd watchdog supervision with
.BR WatchdogSec=30s .
Systemd passes
.B WATCHDOG_USEC
to murald, and murald sends
.B WATCHDOG=1
at half that interval. Use a user-service drop-in with
.B WatchdogSec=0
to disable watchdog recovery locally while diagnosing freezes.
.PP
The supplied unit joins
.BR graphical-session.target
and requires
.B WAYLAND_DISPLAY
in the systemd user manager environment. A compositor or session manager that
does not provide that integration should start the unit from its own session
startup or run murald directly.
.SH FILES
.TP
.I $XDG_CONFIG_HOME/mural/config
Preferred config file when XDG_CONFIG_HOME is set.
.TP
.I ~/.config/mural/config
Fallback config file.
.TP
.I $XDG_STATE_HOME/mural
Preferred state directory.
.TP
.I ~/.local/state/mural
Fallback state directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/mural/mural.sock
Preferred IPC socket location when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is a nonempty absolute path.
.TP
.I /tmp/mural-UID/mural.sock
Owner-only fallback when XDG_RUNTIME_DIR is unavailable. An existing parent
directory must belong to UID and have no group or other permissions. Set
.B MURAL_SOCKET
or pass
.B --socket
to choose an explicit path.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR muralctl (1),
.BR mural-config (5),
.BR systemd.service (5)
